" *.kiritanconfig files (docs/DESIGN.md chapter 3.1) are real ESM JavaScript with no file extension of their own. Unlike the VS Code extension, which registers a distinct "kiritanconfig" language (to keep vscode-icons' language-keyed icon rule from overriding a custom icon — see the VS Code extension's own README for why), Vim/Neovim's ecosystem doesn't force that same tradeoff: setting the real "javascript" filetype directly gets native syntax highlighting, indentation, and any LSP client keyed on "javascript" (e.g. typescript-language-server via nvim-lspconfig) attaching for free, at the cost of no custom file icon — a purely cosmetic loss a devicons plugin's own per-filename overrides can address, the same way vscode-icons' own custom-association setting could.
autocmd BufRead,BufNewFile *.kiritanconfig set filetype=javascript
